  "slug": "tally-credit-note-ledger-check",
  "title": "How to Find a Credit Note in a Customer Ledger",
  "description": "Locate the correct document by voucher type and date before comparing a customer statement with the original books.",
  "category": "Stock and balances",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Find the source credit note",
      "body": "In TallyPrime, note the company, customer, credit note number, date and amount. A customer's invoice and credit note can be recorded on different dates. Check the date of the credit note itself when setting the ledger filter."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Read it in the same period",
      "body": "Open the same party ledger in Syncora and include the credit note date. Find the entry by type and number. If the request is to review a particular invoice, ask the accounting team to confirm the relationship between the documents."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Check the statement impact",
      "body": "Compare the relevant ledger movements and balances with TallyPrime. If the credit note falls outside the exported period, explain that date difference to the reviewer and use the agreed reporting period before re-exporting anything."
    }
  ],
